      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## 3d/world-elements\n\nProp still -> one textured .glb, painted against a ground plate so the asset matches the surface it is going to sit on.\n\nA world in this stack is a set of instanced `.glb` assets plus a `scene.json` layout composed off-line. This graph writes one prop .glb per Run: you instance it and place the instances in that layout. This stack produces no gaussian splat and no captured point cloud - only meshes.\n\nSources: `LoadImage` prop source (structure, shape, and upsample) and `LoadImage` ground plate (the texture pass). Each is gated and unloaded on its own way into the graph, and each runs through its own `Trellis2Conditioning`.\n\nUNET: `trellis_2_int8_convrot.safetensors`. CLIP vision: `dino_v3_vit_l.safetensors` (DINOv3 license, opt-in pack). Structure decode stays at 32.\n\nUpsample `target_resolution` is an int and ComfyUI only accepts 1024-2048 in steps of 128; this graph runs the 1024 floor.\n\nBatch stays 1 and the mesh converts through MeshToFile3D, which keeps only batch item 0. SaveGLB writes the mesh to `output/assets/objects/_lab-world/element_NNNNN_.glb`; MeshToFile3D only converts in memory. Do not mint an Asset Bible row from this graph.\n\n`Compose scene layout` is the second half of this Queue: it writes the `scene.json` that instances the `.glb` slugs already in the Asset Bible, with their placement and one camera, under `output/scenes/`. Its `assets` box takes one slug per line, so you place the set once and refine the rows in the DCC. Blender or a host viewer assembles the scene from that document - see the Blender desk.\n\n`3d/set-dressing` is the App on the handoff: it composes the whole set at once, every slug you have printed, with no mesh printed again.\n\nDINOv3 is Meta's custom commercial-friendly license - not Apache. MIT TRELLIS weights without DINOv3 cannot Queue.\n\nOccupancy: trellis - stop Blender desk, LTX, Wan, Klein denoise. One GB10 job.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Operator note"
    },
