  "config": {},
  "extra": {
    "lab_note": "## 3d/world-elements\n\nProp still -> one textured .glb, painted against a ground plate so the asset matches the surface it is going to sit on.\n\nA world in this stack is a set of instanced `.glb` assets plus a `scene.json` layout composed off-line. This graph writes one prop .glb per Run: you instance it and place the instances in that layout. This stack produces no gaussian splat and no captured point cloud - only meshes.\n\nSources: `LoadImage` prop source (structure, shape, and upsample) and `LoadImage` ground plate (the texture pass). Each is gated and unloaded on its own way into the graph, and each runs through its own `Trellis2Conditioning`.\n\nUNET: `trellis_2_int8_convrot.safetensors`. CLIP vision: `dino_v3_vit_l.safetensors` (DINOv3 license, opt-in pack). Structure decode stays at 32.\n\nUpsample `target_resolution` is an int and ComfyUI only accepts 1024-2048 in steps of 128; this graph runs the 1024 floor.\n\nBatch stays 1 and the mesh converts through MeshToFile3D, which keeps only batch item 0. SaveGLB writes the mesh to `output/assets/objects/_lab-world/element_NNNNN_.glb`; MeshToFile3D only converts in memory. Do not mint an Asset Bible row from this graph.\n\n`Compose scene layout` is the second half of this Queue: it writes the `scene.json` that instances the `.glb` slugs already in the Asset Bible, with their placement and one camera, under `output/scenes/`. Its `assets` box takes one slug per line, so you place the set once and refine the rows in the DCC. Blender or a host viewer assembles the scene from that document - see the Blender desk.\n\n`3d/set-dressing` is the App on the handoff: it composes the whole set at once, every slug you have printed, with no mesh printed again.\n\nDINOv3 is Meta's custom commercial-friendly license - not Apache. MIT TRELLIS weights without DINOv3 cannot Queue.\n\nOccupancy: trellis - stop Blender desk, LTX, Wan, Klein denoise. One GB10 job.\n",
    "lab_profile": "3d/world-elements",
    "lab_description": "Prop still plus a ground plate to one textured TRELLIS.2 .glb for a set.",
    "lab_trellis": {
      "unet": "trellis_2_int8_convrot.safetensors",
      "resolution": 1024,
      "stages": [
        "structure",
        "shape",
        "upsample",
        "texture"
      ],
      "textured": true,
      "batch_size": 1,
      "save_prefix": "assets/objects/_lab-world/element",
      "native_only": true
    },
    "lab_optional_unwired": [
      "EZSceneLayout"
    ],
    "lab_app_mode": {
      "enabled": true,
      "default_view": "app",
      "frontend_min": "1.41.13",
      "lane": "3d",
      "occupancy": "trellis",
      "enhance_off_identity": true,
      "handoff": [
        "3d/set-dressing"
      ]
    },
    "linearData": {
      "inputs": [
        [
          6,
          "image",
          {
            "label": "Prop source",
            "description": "Still already in input/ (the container inputs folder). The prop whose geometry this Run prints."
          }
        ],
        [
          10,
          "image",
          {
            "label": "Ground plate",
            "description": "Still already in input/. The surface the prop will sit on: the texture pass is conditioned on it so the paint matches the real ground."
          }
        ],
        [
          29,
          "quality",
          {
            "label": "Quality",
            "description": "custom freezes the last overlay. lab restores graph defaults. Free Commercial Use (<$10M) is Klein 4B + LTX-2.5 (never Non-Commercial stills). ultra/max may select opt-in Non-Commercial weights when on disk. Family-specific - not --tier."
          }
        ],
        [
          19,
          "target_resolution",
          {
            "label": "Upsample resolution",
            "description": "Structure resolution the refined shape stage renders at. ComfyUI accepts only 1024-2048 in steps of 128; 1024 is the floor and the lab default."
          }
        ],
        [
          23,
          "steps",
          {
            "label": "Texture pass",
            "description": "Steps on the texture sampler. 12 is the authored pass; 4-6 is a paint draft before you commit the full pass. The mesh geometry does not change."
          }
        ],
        [
          27,
          "filename_prefix",
          {
            "label": "Save prefix",
            "description": "Output stem under the ComfyUI output folder. Keep the assets/objects/_lab-... convention so the mesh lands in the one tree the catalog and the Blender exporter walk."
          }
        ],
        [
          18,
          "steps",
          {
            "label": "Shape steps",
            "description": "Steps on the structure-refinement sampler. A proxy reads fine at 8; 12 is the authored pass for a deliverable."
          }
        ],
        [
          28,
          "assets",
          {
            "label": "Scene assets",
            "description": "One Asset Bible slug per line. The layout document instances these slugs; an unknown slug leaves the file unwritten and the summary line says why."
          }
        ],
        [
          28,
          "camera_pos",
          {
            "label": "Camera position",
            "description": "\"x, y, z\" in metres. Blank falls back to the camera default in schemas/scene.json."
          }
        ],
        [
          28,
          "hdri",
          {
            "label": "HDRI",
            "description": "polyhaven:<name> or none. The document records the lighting reference the DCC loads; none keeps the viewer's default."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "outputs": [
        27,
        28
      ]
    },
    "linearMode": true,
    "lab_quality": {
      "default": "lab"
    },
    "lab_rel": "3d/world-elements",
    "workflowRendererVersion": "Vue-corrected"
  },
  "version": 0.4
